<title>LITHUANIA: SNORAS ASSETS 448 MLN LITAS AT END JUNE.</title>
<headline>SNORAS ASSETS 448 MLN LITAS AT END JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's Snoras Bank said on Monday its assets rose to 448 million litas at the end of June from 425 million litas at the end of May but fell compared with 552 million litas at the end of 1996.  </p>
<p>The bank did not give a precise reason for the fall in assets from December to June.</p>
<p>&quot;The main reason (for the fall) is interbank relations,&quot; Gintaras Radvila, director of Snoras Bank's marketing department, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Banks do not just go up all the time,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Burton Frierson, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 18</p>
</text>
